From d34e482563a8d8c422e5449a7b90e3fae98696ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:18:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix O(sheet-size) cell lookups; add the worker pool
 (D134, D37)

PERF-01/05: Sheet._cells (grid-window query) and the sheets' extent
both scanned every cell in the sheet on every call, so a document's
cost tracked its total size instead of the size of what was asked
for. Sheet now maintains a sparse row-to-sorted-columns index plus
lazy-deletion max-heaps for the row/column extent, kept incrementally
at WorkbookModel.store()'s single per-cell mutation point; the
existing full-rebuild path is kept only for structural edits and
document load (Sheet.refit()). claudia_server.computes now calls
cells_in()/extent() instead of scanning. Verified both for
correctness (40 random set/clear cycles compared against a naive
full-scan reference, undo, snapshot reload, structural edits) and for
cost (scaling guards comparing a 10k-cell sheet against a 500k-cell
one, added to check_debt.py's perf tuple).

D134/D37: adds WorkerPool, a generic submit(fn, *args, **kwargs) over
a ProcessPoolExecutor bridged into asyncio, with crash isolation (a
worker process dying outright no longer breaks the pool for other
work). Hub owns one instance as Hub.workers, started and stopped with
the Hub. Public API bumped to 0.9.0 (WorkerPool, DEFAULT_WORKERS,
Hub's new max_workers parameter), with CHANGELOG, docs and the
api_surface snapshot updated to match.

